Just had my best character to date, level 23, 205 HP, die instantly
when went up a staircase and found myself in a small room with 
MEDUSA.  This was my first character powerful enough to go down
this far, and having never been this far I was hoping a few of
you more experienced hackers could answer some questions...

When I entered level 27, there was some floor, then alot of
water with some electric eels.  Put on my towel, and saw alot
of monsters across the water.  Didn't have water walking boots,
and wasn't sure if a ring of levitation would get me across or
if I would come crashing down (as when passing over a sink)
into the drink.

* Do rings of levitation get you across bodies of water?


Tried to teleport, but some mysterious force prevented me.

* Is this natural for this level, or did I do something wrong?


Decided to play it safe, took out my pick-axe and dug down,
falling to the level below.  Level 28 was a huge maze.

* Does this signify I entered a new part of the dungeon 
  (I assume I was in the Dungeons of Doom before the maze)?

* And, how do you (short of dying) tell where in the dungeon
  you are?  

* A while ago, someone posted an nice concise description of 
  the dungeon, average levels and what to expect where...anyone 
  still have it to re-post?


Wandered around for a while until I hit a trap and polymorphed
into a Red Dragon, destroying my elven mithril coat, Hawaiian
Shirt and Cloak of Protection in the process (forgot to remove
my ring of adornment and replace the ring of polymorph control,
which inspired my previous post).  Later, after I returned to
samurai form, I found the up staircase, went up straight to my 
instant 205/205 HP to stone-dead death (oh the joys of nethack).  

I recall seeing a small room with at least one statue and the @
nearby, but everything in my mind became a blur and I'm not sure 
of the details.  It seems that once I arrived at the top of the 
stairs into MEDUSA's room, I had one turn before she nailed me 
(or is this my slow-motion recollection of my last moment of life).

* Once you enter the room with MEDUSA, do you get any turns
  or are you instantly stoned (was wearing blessed speed boots,
  if that matters).

I recall our long, agonizing battle went something like this:
--the MEDUSA gazes at you
--her gaze is reflected back by your shield of reflection
--you look at the MEDUSA
--you turn to stone

* Is there anything short of being blind (blindfold, towel, etc)
  which would have saved me?  (I had a wand of death, if only I'd
  known).

* Is the MEDUSA always in a room at the top of a staircase?  (I'd
  hate to have to blind myself before ascending every staircase,
